# =============================================================================
# Climate Brain v1.3.4.1 — sole writer for two communicating HVAC zones
# Generated. Household entity IDs come from the wizard, not this template.
# Phase 1 + Phase 2 in ONE operational automation / ONE writer.
# Precool, slope EMA, night, late arrival, morning live here together.
# 1.3.1: travel delta is latch-aware (comfort_cool when cool).
#         Precool cancel if still toward but ETA > lead+5 min (hysteresis).
#         Turn-around (not toward) still cancels immediately.
# 1.3.2: log iCloud3 dir/ETA/zone + Tesla if present; no lat/lon; tesla never occupancy.
# 1.3.3: File logger removed (Home Assistant would not register that notify from YAML).
#         Logs go to home-assistant.log via system_log.write logger=climate_brain.
#
# Writes ONLY:
#   __Z1__  (Zone 1)
#   __Z2__  (Zone 2)
# NEVER versatile_thermostat.*
# NEVER climate.home_thermostat / climate.home_thermostat_2
# NEVER hvac_mode auto (Auto = wall schedule → 62/82). Occupied / late_hold /
#   night = heat_cool (target_temp_low/high). Boost / precool / vacation_boost
#   = latched heat OR cool + single boost temp (73 heat or 70 cool). Empty /
#   vacation = latched heat OR cool + away/vacation temp. NEVER inverted dual.
#
# Precool starts only while __OCCUPANCY__ is off.
# Occupancy on (or unknown) never starts precool. Occupancy on cancels it.
# Arrival lockout: input_number.climate_brain_arrival_lockout_min (default 10 min).
# Vacation: input_boolean.climate_brain_vacation forces latched heat/cool at
#   vacation setpoints (presence conceptually away). No initial: HA restores it.
#   Real occupancy-on clears it and starts vacation_boost, not late_hold.
#   Vacation off: ALWAYS script.climate_brain_vacation_boost_start even if empty.
#   Boost until both zones reach the comfort band, or 2h safety. Then
#   occupancy / travel / clock. Occupancy_off does NOT cancel vacation_boost.
# Clock backups: template triggers at night/morning/day HH:MM so 5:15 still
# fires after a YAML reload. Occupancy unknown never writes Away.
# Power loss: last_write is the snapshot. Gap > 5 min cancels leftover timers,
# then clock+occupancy. Vacation boolean restores.
#
# Tesla is optional and travel/ETA only (never occupancy). CAN readers
# only (never a trigger, never a write). Do not add them to occupancy.
# travel_snap logs Tesla device_trackers/sensors via states() if present
# (entity_id=state, no lat/lon). Tesla is NEVER an occupancy trigger.
#
# INSTALL
#   1. Put this file at config/packages/climate_brain.yaml
#   2. In configuration.yaml:
#        homeassistant:
#          packages: !include_dir_named packages
#   3. Also in configuration.yaml (if not already). Do not put a global
#      logger: block in this package — merge is unreliable:
#        logger:
#          default: warning
#          logs:
#            climate_brain: info
#   4. Disable or remove both Versatile Thermostat instances
#      (climate.home_thermostat / climate.home_thermostat_2). Brain writes Trane only.
#   5. Dashboard: Zone 1 / Zone 2 only. Hide extra VTherm cards.
#   6. Full HA restart (not yaml reload) so helpers/timers/scripts exist.
#   7. Logs: home-assistant.log, search climate_brain (logger: climate_brain: info).
#      Attach matching lines in chat. Do not use notify.file.
#   8. UNINSTALL: turn off climate_brain_enabled, delete this file, restart HA,
#      purge leftover climate_brain* entities.
#
# NEVER writes climate.home_thermostat*. NEVER calls versatile_thermostat.*.
# NEVER writes CAN frames. NEVER uses time_pattern polling. NEVER sets auto.
# =============================================================================

